The heavier INSAT and GSAT communication satellites were long launched on Europe's **Ariane** rockets from **Kourou** (French Guiana) because India's own GSLV could not lift them; **LVM3** (GSLV Mk III) now launches about 4 tonnes to geosynchronous transfer orbit from Sriharikota. **INSAT-4C** (2,168 kg) was lost when GSLV-F02 failed in July 2006. **RISAT-2** (2009, Israeli-built radar imager) watches borders day and night; **ANUSAT** was Anna University's student satellite.

