@qnote 13:54 | The source gives **(c) & (d)**: **Mars** has traces of methane (seen by Curiosity and Mars Express), and **Jupiter**'s atmosphere has about 0.3% methane along with hydrogen and helium.

**Methane** colours **Uranus and Neptune** blue-green; the giant planets are mostly hydrogen and helium. NASA's airborne telescope **SOFIA** confirmed water molecules on the sunlit Moon (2020). In 2018 Italian scientists using radar on ESA's Mars Express reported a **lake of liquid water under the Martian south polar ice**.

